\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {IV.4}{\ignorespaces Evolution of the activation fraction of three INAS parametrisations, against temperature and particle diameter in semi-logarithmic scale. The $\gamma $ factor is not yet applied here, so all reach \SI {100}{\percent } activation. The inclinaison of the threshold lines accounts for the relative weight of particle diameter and temperature for the activation fraction. The saturated darker zones show the parameter space for which the parametrisations predict between \SI {10}{\percent } and full activation. Panel A is H18B (bacteria), B is M18 (sea sprays) and C is N12 (dust).}}{122}{figure.caption.81}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:activation_fraction}{{IV.4}{122}{Evolution of the activation fraction of three INAS parametrisations, against temperature and particle diameter in semi-logarithmic scale. The $\gamma $ factor is not yet applied here, so all reach \perc {100} activation. The inclinaison of the threshold lines accounts for the relative weight of particle diameter and temperature for the activation fraction. The saturated darker zones show the parameter space for which the parametrisations predict between \perc {10} and full activation. Panel A is H18B (bacteria), B is M18 (sea sprays) and C is N12 (dust)}{figure.caption.81}{}}
